# What never enters the build context.

# ─── CORRECTNESS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `bcrypt` resolves a PLATFORM binary at install time and this tree is developed on
# Windows, so a host `node_modules/` carries `bcrypt/prebuilds/win32-x64`. Copying it
# into a linux image produces a container that starts and then throws on the first
# password hash. `npm ci` runs INSIDE the image for exactly this reason.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# `ADMIN_AUDIT_EXPORT_DIR` defaults to `./var/audit-exports` — a RUNTIME OUTPUT path
# holding the exported NDJSON that the audit retention chain points at. Plan D-7: it
# is a named volume mounted at /app/var/audit-exports, never an image layer. Baking a
# developer's export runs into the image would ship real audit rows to every host, and
# an image that loses them leaves audit records stamped `exported` pointing at nothing.
# This is a second instance of ADR-019 D-1a, which names only jovi-mall's uploads.
var

# ─── SECRETS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Compose supplies the container's environment. `.env.example` is kept: it documents
# the contract and carries no secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── BUILD OUTPUT AND NOISE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The builder stage produces dist/ itself; a host copy is a Windows-built artefact of
# unknown vintage shadowing it.
dist

.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage

# Documentation, including the ADR set. Large, and no code path reads it.
docs
*.md
